# Supported features

@NAME@ contains a shared C23 greeting model, a console frontend and an optional
GTK4 window. Enter a name and create a greeting. The same validation is used by
both frontends. This is a working starter application for your own features.

# Getting started

1. Read the root README for SDK, build and test instructions.
2. Add business behaviour to `src/model.c` and declare it in `src/model.h`.
3. Extend `tests/test_model.c` with expected results and invalid-input cases.
4. Call the model from the frontend and show errors to the user.
5. Keep this guide accurate as you add capabilities.

# Limitations

There are no account connections, persistent documents, background services,
web frontend or mobile frontend in this starter. GTK4 needs its development
package. The console-only manifest does not advertise a native GUI. To add that
frontend later, add its manifest declarations, give the console a distinct
executable name, and update the CMake capability check and option together.
